   "about": "A historical account of Japanese labor, agrarian and minority movements, nationalist politics, and the revival of parties and unions after 1945.",
   "summary": "The report’s continuing chapter on labor and farmers’ organizations describes their divisions, repression and absorption into wartime patriotic bodies. Chapter VII examines the history of discrimination against the Buraku minority, the Suiheisha movement, protest incidents and 1946 population figures. Chapter VIII follows nationalist parties and the Imperial Rule Assistance Association through the suppression of liberal and left-wing opposition. Chapter IX begins an account of the political freedoms introduced after surrender and the reestablishment of socialist and communist parties and labor unions; it continues beyond this section.",
